{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03338",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.73,
      "end_seconds": 7.04,
      "duration_seconds": 6.31,
      "text": "Doctor, your next patient is here. I've done the basics, I'll read them out in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.87,
      "end_seconds": 13.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Thank you. Right, hello, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.78,
      "end_seconds": 25.23,
      "duration_seconds": 10.45,
      "text": "It's a high sugar test in pregnancy, mostly. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.01,
      "end_seconds": 30.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Alright, has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.33,
      "end_seconds": 35.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "I've had it for four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.7,
      "end_seconds": 41.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.13,
      "end_seconds": 43.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "It's severe, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.53,
      "end_seconds": 47.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.01,
      "end_seconds": 61.16,
      "duration_seconds": 13.15,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get a big baby on the scan as well. The big baby on the scan? That's been for four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.2,
      "end_seconds": 66.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Any thirst or passing a lot of urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.07,
      "end_seconds": 70.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "No, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.72,
      "end_seconds": 76.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Have you had any reduced baby movements or blurred vision?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.75,
      "end_seconds": 82.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "No, no reduced baby movements or blurred vision."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.85,
      "end_seconds": 87.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Right, right. Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.37,
      "end_seconds": 90.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "No, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.04,
      "end_seconds": 108.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.96,
      "end_seconds": 128.68,
      "duration_seconds": 18.72,
      "text": "I'll have a glass of wine with dinner. I quit smoking around ten years ago. Not much, I mostly stay in these days. I look after my grandchildren most days. I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.62,
      "end_seconds": 132.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "So, have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.59,
      "end_seconds": 136.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "No surgery, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.93,
      "end_seconds": 142.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.81,
      "end_seconds": 148.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Yes, nickel. I get a rash on my skin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.03,
      "end_seconds": 152.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.18,
      "end_seconds": 156.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "I take propranolol, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.83,
      "end_seconds": 160.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.96,
      "end_seconds": 165.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "40 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.6,
      "end_seconds": 173.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.22,
      "end_seconds": 175.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Yes, migraines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.64,
      "end_seconds": 180.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Okay, I can see migraines in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 188.46,
      "end_seconds": 204.31,
      "duration_seconds": 15.85,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Height 171 centimetres, pulse is 84 beats a minute, oxygen saturation is 97 percent, BMI works out to 25.6, temperature is 36.6 degrees, BP is 122 over 77, weight 75 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.82,
      "end_seconds": 207.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.2,
      "end_seconds": 213.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.84,
      "end_seconds": 225.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.64,
      "end_seconds": 229.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.41,
      "end_seconds": 251.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "Your blood pressure is normal and your urine has no sugar today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.13,
      "end_seconds": 265.39,
      "duration_seconds": 9.26,
      "text": "You can sit up now. Okay, so my impression is this: This is probably gestational diabetes controllable with diet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.33,
      "end_seconds": 271.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.91,
      "end_seconds": 299.49,
      "duration_seconds": 26.58,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with gestational diabetes controllable with diet do well once it's treated properly. I'm sending you for a growth scan because of gestational diabetes. I'll request a glucose meter and diary, it'll help with gestational diabetes. Replace sugary drinks and white starches with wholegrains and walk after meals. See me again in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.14,
      "end_seconds": 304.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "That's fine with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.76,
      "end_seconds": 312.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.95,
      "end_seconds": 315.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Great, thank you for your help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.85,
      "end_seconds": 319.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}